# Snapshot and golden files are compared byte-for-byte by tests, and are written by
# tools (vitest, scripts/balance.ts) that always emit LF. With core.autocrlf on,
# git would check them out as CRLF on Windows, so the golden test would fail on any
# fresh clone and every regenerated snapshot would read as dirty in `git status`.
#
# Pinning them to LF makes the checked-out bytes match what the tools produce.
tests/__snapshots__/** text eol=lf
